    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0887" n="877" xml:id="pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commander of the Seventh Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cooke</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to General Marshall
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-05">5 October 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>030210Z. Withdrawal of Marines from bridge, coal mine and train guard duty
                    completed 30 Sept. In each case relief was made by CNA forces. Marines now
                    concentrated Peiping, Tientsin–Taku, Peitaiho–Chinwangtao and Tsingtao. My
                        040538Z<anchor n="67" xml:id="d586-f1"/> refers.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d586-f1" n="67" xml:id="d586-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram of September 5, not printed.</p>
